.\" gencat.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX gencat(1) utility, which
.\" this tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/GENCAT.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/GENCAT.
.TH GENCAT 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
gencat \- generate a formatted message catalog
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Gencat
is not provided on maux.
maux supports only the C locale: a 7-bit ASCII character set,
with the high bit reserved for this system's own text-file
convention rather than a second locale. There is no other locale
to select, generate, or translate messages for.
